# Build-context hygiene. Without this, `docker build` ships ~1.35 GB to
# package a 1.9 MB corpus: 936 MB of node_modules, a 244 MB host .venv built
# for macOS, and a 96 MB local ledger. Everything excluded here is either
# rebuilt inside the image, machine-local, or a secret.

# Version control and tooling
.git
.github
.gitignore
.claude
.agents
.impeccable
.pytest_cache
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[co]

# Host-built dependency trees — wrong platform for the image, and huge
.venv
**/node_modules
dashboard/dist

# Secrets. .env.example is the template that ships; .env never does.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Runtime state. The ledger is rebuilt from the corpus on first boot (0.3s),
# uploads and drafts belong to whoever runs the container, and the reseed
# backup is a local artifact that isn't even tracked by git.
# Every SQLite file and JSONL export under data/ is runtime state or a local
# snapshot, never something the image should carry. Narrower patterns rotted:
# `data/ledger.db` alone let 66 MB of ledger-previous / ledger-backup copies
# into the image, and only because they are untracked did CI (which builds
# from a git checkout) produce a different, smaller image than a local build.
data/*.db
data/*.jsonl
data/uploads
registry/drafts

# Docs and tests aren't needed to run the service
docs
eval
tests

# Working-tree-only files: not in git, so a local build would otherwise bake
# in what CI cannot see, and the two would stop being the same image. None of
# them is read at runtime.
CLAUDE.md
DESIGN.md
PLAN.md
DEMO-RUNBOOK.md
skills-lock.json
scripts/make_intake_demo.py
scripts/rebuild_ledger.py
